{
  "id": "phase-120",
  "title": "Let the REPL pipe to the shell and bind keys, without loading code",
  "severity": "minor",
  "depends_on": [],
  "risk": "medium",
  "finding": "Two things Ipp has and Redblue does not, kept deliberately apart because they differ in risk. `:pipe` runs a shell command from the session (Ipp REPL_AUDIT.md 2.28); Redblue has no equivalent, so checking a file or running a build means leaving the REPL and losing the session's bindings. `:bind` maps keys to commands (2.29). Neither is a language feature, but both are the difference between a REPL you live in and one you tolerate. Ipp's `:plugin` (2.33), which loads code into the session at runtime, is NOT in this phase: executing untrusted code with no gate is the exact surface AGENTS.md rule 2 forbids, and a gated pipeline should not build the capability even if a sibling project can afford it.",
  "goal": "Add `:pipe <shell command>` running the command as the user typed it and capturing its combined output, and `:bind <key> <command>` mapping a key to any existing command. Scope `:pipe` to read-only commands and say so in the help text; this is a convenience for inspecting, not a shell replacement. Skip `:plugin` entirely and record in FINDINGS.md that it was considered and declined, so a later phase does not re-propose it without reading why.",
  "accept": [
    "`:pipe <command>` runs it and prints stdout and stderr, with a non-zero exit reported rather than swallowed",
    "a command that does not exist is reported as such, not as empty output",
    "`:pipe` with no argument raises a catchable error rather than running an empty command",
    "`:bind <key> <command>` makes that key run that command, and a rebound key replaces rather than stacks",
    "binding an unknown command raises a catchable error naming it at bind time, not at press time",
    "`:bind` with no arguments lists every current binding in deterministic order",
    "a key bound to a command that produces output shows that output through the normal colour path",
    "FINDINGS.md records that `:plugin` was considered and declined, with the AGENTS.md rule it would violate",
    "edge_* cases cover a command producing no output, a command with a non-zero exit, a pipe to a command that reads stdin, and a key bound to itself"
  ],
  "timeout_min": 150
}
