    - comparison operators lex and compare (`==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`) - MET, verified at runtime this audit: `say (1 == 1)` prints yes, `say (1 != 2)` yes, `say (1 < 2)` yes, `say (2 <= 2)` yes, `say (2 > 1)` yes, `say (2 >= 2)` yes; all exit 0. The old entry claimed `say 1 == 1` raises LexerError: Unexpected character `=` - that is no longer true and was removed rather than left as a warning
  - `break` exits its loop - MET, verified at runtime this audit: over [1,2,3,4,5], breaking at 3 leaves the counter at 2. The old entry claimed `Statement::Break` is a TODO no-op in src/interpreter.rs - it is not; phase-025 landed it
  - range loops (`for each i from A to B`) - MET, verified at runtime this audit: `for each i from 1 to 4` summing gives 10; `... from 0 to 10 by 2` gives 30
  - `unless` blocks - MET, verified at runtime this audit: `unless x is 0 then say "nonzero" end` prints nonzero. Note `then` is required (docs/GRAMMAR.md:236); omitting it is a ParserError, not a missing feature
  - `module`/`export`/`import` for compiler structure - MET, verified at runtime this audit: `import math` then `math.sqrt(9)` prints 3, and `import math as m` then `m.sqrt(9)` prints 3
  - function literals as expressions, for emitting functions - MET, verified at runtime this audit: `set double to to (x) return x * 2 end` then `say double(21)` prints 42
  - NOT a bootstrap blocker but a live correctness defect the compiler will inherit: `this` is not accepted as the operand of `at`/`of` - src/parser.rs:1813 omits TokenKind::This from kind_starts_operand while src/parser.rs:2575 parses it as a primary, so `length of this` is a ParserError and `this.xs at this` misparses as `Unknown variable at`. Tracked as phase-110.
  - NOT a bootstrap blocker but a live correctness defect the compiler will inherit: `else if` does not parse in any position - src/parser.rs:791 has no else-if arm, so the nested if steals the outer `end`. Documented at SPEC.md:391 and docs/GRAMMAR.md:221. Tracked as phase-112.
